1
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,760
(18+ viewers only)

2
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,280
(18+ viewers only
(May contain disturbing content)

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,440
(Contains violence, sex,
and strong language)

4
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,760
(This series is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual person, place, organization, or event.)

5
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,160
(During the production process, AI technology was used in certain scenes to support on-set safety,)

6
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,040
(as well as to enhance the quality and realism of the visual presentation.)

7
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,000
Inspector.

8
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,720
What's that on your lips?

9
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,960
(Like heck it is.)

10
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,720
(I was stupid to trust you.)

11
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,560
(Was messing with my feelings)

12
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,800
(fun for you?)

13
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,520
(Did you ever think about how I'd feel?)

14
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,880
(I thought you trusted me.)

15
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,920
(I thought we trusted each other.)

16
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,400
(Can I stay here?)

17
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,400
(I don't care what role I have.)

18
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,200
(Just let me stay here,)

19
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,840
(by your side.)

20
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,760
(WeTV Original Series)

21
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:32,760
=Nour=
(WeTV Original)

22
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:45,800
Nin, come here.

23
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,120
Okay.

24
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:49,760
What is it?

25
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:55,920
Is it

26
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,920
study notes?

27
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,360
Thanks.

28
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,400
I know what you're worried about.

29
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,160
But don't worry this time.

30
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,240
I won't repeat that mistake.

31
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,000
I...

32
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,160
I'm sorry

33
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,880
for barging into your room
the other day.

34
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,800
I was just worried about you.

35
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,720
I was afraid it'd happen again.

36
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,120
Don't worry.

37
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,080
If I date someone again,

38
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,120
I won't repeat that mistake.

39
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:25,640
Trust me.

40
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,080
Okay.

41
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,480
Focus on your studies,

42
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,400
so if anything ever happens to me,

43
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,880
you're able to look after Mom.

44
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,240
Here.

45
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,440
Study notes.

46
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,640
It's faded a lot.

47
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,440
I told you, I'm fine now.

48
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,640
I meant the writing's faded.

49
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:49,560
I might not be able to read it.

50
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,400
It's fine. This is probably
what'll be on the test.

51
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:55,360
Thanks.

52
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,640
Besides Rain,

53
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,320
you're all I have.

54
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,200
It's okay.

55
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,200
It's okay.

56
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:18,880
Go on.

57
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:19,840
Go study.

58
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,080
Thanks.

59
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,120
Inspector.

60
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,520
Are you okay?

61
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,120
What's wrong, Officer?

62
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,760
(Authorized Personnel Only)

63
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,640
Trust me.

64
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,480
We need to clear this up.

65
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,120
You still won't let this case go?

66
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,680
I'd love to see the world
through your eyes.

67
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,560
Your world is fine as it is.

68
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,480
Why would you want to see mine?

69
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:03,600
What?

70
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,360
Packing.

71
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,640
I'm going back where I belong.

72
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,640
What happened just now?

73
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:21,680
Nothing happened.

74
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,480
Just leave me alone.

75
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,120
Before...

76
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,640
why did you treat me like that?

77
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,480
I...

78
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,120
Take responsibility for what you did.

79
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,080
Responsibility?

80
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,600
For what?

81
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,200
You're the one who sent me away.

82
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,320
Why are you messing with me now?

83
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,520
How am I supposed to trust you again?

84
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,720
- Oh my God.
- You scared me!

85
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,080
So sweet.

86
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:25,920
Oh my gosh.

87
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,160
(Authorized Personnel Only)

88
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:30,840
He's really mad now.

89
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:31,920
What do we do?

90
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,600
Don't finish it.

91
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:38,720
(Authorized Personnel Only)

92
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:43,800
(Criminal Investigation Division)

93
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:45,840
Inspector.

94
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,440
James.

95
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,680
Don't go.

96
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,600
It's not up to me.

97
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,600
I know.

98
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:03,520
But...

99
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,040
ever since you came here,

100
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,400
this station has changed a lot.

101
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,960
Everyone's been working harder

102
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,040
and showing more initiative.

103
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,600
Even Phong has changed.

104
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,760
Not to mention Inspector Ken.

105
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,080
He is the one

106
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,160
changed most.

107
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,600
Who would've thought

108
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,160
James could get Inspector Ken
to go to a bar?

109
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:29,640
Inspector Ken...

110
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,400
So what if he's changed?

111
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,920
Don't forget,

112
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,320
he's the one who sent me away.

113
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,360
What do you expect me to do?

114
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,200
James.

115
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,160
Why leave without saying goodbye?

116
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,080
If something's wrong, talk to us.

117
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:46,600
Come on.

118
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,240
Sit down and talk.

119
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,040
What's wrong?

120
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,400
Still, I think

121
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,800
Inspector Ken must have his reasons.

122
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,280
Why don't you talk to him first?

123
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,600
I used to date someone too.

124
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,160
And...

125
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:13,480
we fought all the time.

126
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,160
But we always talked things out right away.

127
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:16,600
Really.

128
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,080
I used to date someone too.

129
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,480
It's normal.

130
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:21,360
Dating?

131
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,680
We're not like that.

132
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,480
Not like what?

133
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:25,640
We all know that.

134
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,240
Exactly.

135
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:29,960
Forget it.

136
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,240
But right now,

137
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:33,720
I'm really confused.

138
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,400
About what?

139
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,560
If you don't trust your partner,

140
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,840
what would you do?

141
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,360
For me,

142
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,360
I'd find out the truth first.

143
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,760
Then I'd go straight to them

144
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,160
and talk it out.

145
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,000
Exactly.

146
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,080
That's what you should do.

147
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:58,360
The truth...

148
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:03,960
Tangme.

149
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,880
Do you have Inspector Ken's address?

150
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,280
Doctor.

151
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,400
Are you okay?

152
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:21,960
Why do you look so down?

153
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,040
Actually,

154
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:26,080
shouldn't you be happy that no one's
bothering you anymore?

155
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,640
Now you can keep investigating.

156
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:28,800
I've always been like this.

157
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,680
Rigor mortis.

158
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:37,040
It's hard to find someone

159
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,360
who truly understands you.

160
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,680
Sending him to HQ is for the best.

161
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,280
It's better for him,

162
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:49,920
and for me.

163
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,400
Are you worried

164
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,760
he'll get hurt?

165
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,640
I'm close to finding
the Nour I've been hunting.

166
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,160
While he's here,

167
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,000
he'll try to get rid of it.

168
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,120
Then I may never be able to die.

169
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,280
Still, part of me hopes

170
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,320
you never find it.

171
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,360
I want you to keep living.

172
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:21,840
I've already lived too long.

173
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,000
He's been dead for 12 hours.

174
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:26,640
Note that.

175
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:33,960
Mm.

176
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,240
I'm taking Chita out to eat tomorrow.

177
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,120
If you're free,

178
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,160
join us.

179
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:40,920
Maybe not.

180
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,240
Ready for a fresh start, Dr. Ji?

181
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:47,200
Yes.

182
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:48,720
Good.

183
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,440
Take care of yourself.

184
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,320
Don't work too hard.

185
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,480
You too.

186
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,240
Take care of yourself.

187
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,600
Maybe it's better he's gone.

188
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,080
(The Nour That Can Kill Nour)

189
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:16,000
(Police Station)

190
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,480
Excuse me.

191
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,960
James left without saying goodbye.

192
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,320
He shouldn't have been transferred,
right, Inspector?

193
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,400
What is it, Officer Phong?

194
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,640
A memo from the chief.

195
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,520
Leave it there.

196
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,000
Several recent cases

197
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,160
have already been closed.

198
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:54,960
And this one...

199
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,840
we probably still wouldn't have solved it
without James.

200
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,000
Right?

201
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,160
By the way,

202
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,920
what's the plan for those Nour ghosts?

203
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,080
If James were still here,

204
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,480
it'd probably be much easier,

205
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:13,560
right?

206
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,720
- James could help.
- Don't worry.

207
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,680
I'll handle it myself from here.

208
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,320
Just keep it between us.

209
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,640
You can go.

210
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,440
Understood.

211
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,760
Where did James go?

212
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:46,520
(Regarding the conduct of
Superintendent Nainet Inthakan)

213
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:57,040
(Superintendent Kiran Amatanathi)

214
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,840
Chita, my mom isn't scary.

215
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:08,920
Really, Dr. Ji?

216
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,280
My mom would be happy

217
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,560
that I'm finally home for dinner.

218
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,600
Nin.

219
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,000
Your brother's home.

220
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,640
Hello, ma'am.

221
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:30,600
Mom, this is...

222
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,240
Chita.

223
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,280
My friend

224
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,320
and...

225
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:35,720
assistant.

226
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:37,840
Come in, kid.

227
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:38,960
Stay for dinner.

228
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,400
I'll go get the food ready.

229
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,000
Okay.

230
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,960
Ji, take your friend inside.

231
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,360
Okay.

232
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:43,680
Let's go.

233
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,400
Come on.

234
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,280
Come on.

235
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:47,840
Quit messing around.

236
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:49,920
Leave your shoes here.

237
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,400
Let's go.

238
00:16:59,080 --> 00:16:59,600
Put them here.

239
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:12,800
I made traditional curry today.

240
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,400
Okay.

241
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,560
Mom, why'd you make so much food?

242
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,760
You hardly ever come home. Eat up.

243
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,400
Mom.

244
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,520
My friend loves cooking, just like you.

245
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:34,320
Perfect.

246
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,840
Next time, come help me cook.

247
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,360
Sure.

248
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:44,120
Thanks.

249
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,840
Eat up, both of you.

250
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,600
It tastes even better than usual.

251
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,240
Mom's just worried about you.

252
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,240
You're at the hospital all day,
and I never hear a thing.

253
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:58,880
I don't know how you're doing

254
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,320
or how busy work is.

255
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:02,800
He's all grown up.

256
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,720
You should worry about me.

257
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,680
You have plenty of friends.

258
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:11,640
Rain's my only friend.

259
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:16,480
Since Baifern came by last time,

260
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,560
no one else has visited.

261
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:22,200
Your brother hardly brings anyone home.

262
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,320
Mom, why bring that up now?

263
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,800
He's moved on.

264
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,520
It's good that he has a friend.

265
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,200
He's better off staying single.

266
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,640
Relationships end sooner or later.

267
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,080
Friends can stay in your life longer.

268
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,240
That's much better.

269
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:44,720
Keep eating, kid.

270
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:45,920
Is it good?

271
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,080
What?

272
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:48,080
You have so much left.

273
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,600
Don't you like my cooking?

274
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,280
It's delicious.

275
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:53,120
I just...

276
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:55,080
got caught up listening to you.

277
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,680
Okay, okay. Eat up.

278
00:18:58,760 --> 00:18:59,240
Okay.

279
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,120
How's college?

280
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,200
Pretty good.

281
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:14,720
Lots of exams lately.

282
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,480
You're never around.
I wanted you to tutor me.

283
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,000
What good is being a doctor?

284
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:27,000
Your brother already works hard enough.

285
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:29,800
- He's hardly home.
- Sorry.

286
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,800
I need to use the restroom.

287
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:33,240
Sure. It's right inside, kid.

288
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,680
I'll go check on Chita.

289
00:19:58,520 --> 00:19:58,920
Chita?

290
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,120
Chita?

291
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:06,200
Chita, are you okay?

292
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:09,720
Are you okay?

293
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:10,280
I'm fine.

294
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,200
Next time, you have to tell me

295
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:17,880
what you can't eat.

296
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,000
Thanks.

297
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,120
Sorry I didn't tell you before.

298
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,200
Don't blame yourself. It's my fault.

299
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,640
I should've asked you.

300
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:32,880
Then...

301
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,720
let's have dinner again sometime.

302
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:39,120
Okay.

303
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:42,840
How are you feeling, Chita?

304
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:46,320
This is all the medicine we have.

305
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,560
Take this for now.

306
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:47,960
Let me.

307
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:48,960
I'm so sorry.

308
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:51,280
I didn't know you were allergic.

309
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:52,400
It's okay, ma'am.

310
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:53,960
I just

311
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,360
can't really eat curry.

312
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:56,480
I'm sorry.

313
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,120
Thanks.

314
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,400
Okay.

315
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:00,840
Mom, I've got him.

316
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,120
Wipe your hands.

317
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:10,840
Give me your hand.

318
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,840
This is my favorite tree.

319
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:51,480
I've never seen one before.

320
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,280
It's called a sal tree.

321
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:55,840
A sal tree?

322
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,040
It symbolizes

323
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,480
an ending

324
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:07,440
and...

325
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,440
a new beginning.

326
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:13,600
Chita.

327
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:18,440
Are you okay today?

328
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,840
Mom must be happy that I'm
finally home for dinner.

329
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:26,360
I'm fine.

330
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:30,720
I'm worried...

331
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:34,680
I might make your mom
and brother uncomfortable.

332
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:38,080
They'll be fine.

333
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:47,200
But...

334
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:51,920
I'm the one

335
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:55,680
who should apologize.
I can't tell Mom about us.

336
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:59,200
She doesn't want me dating anyone.

337
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,640
Why doesn't your mom want you to date?

338
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:18,200
Fern.

339
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:25,680
I...

340
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:31,600
I'm sorry.

341
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,480
I really can't go with you.

342
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,040
But that doesn't mean

343
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,000
I don't love you.

344
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,000
I'll find a way

345
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,400
to work this out.

346
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:57,000
Fern.

347
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:02,120
Don't make me choose.

348
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,920
You know you're all I have
besides my mom.

349
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,720
I know.

350
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:16,240
But I've thought about this
for a long time.

351
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,280
I'm sorry.

352
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:25,440
If I can't leave,
then stay here with me.

353
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:26,400
Fern, I'm begging you.

354
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:28,000
Fern, let me be selfish this once.

355
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:28,520
Fern.

356
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:46,680
I was devastated back then.

357
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,160
My mind went blank.

358
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:52,800
I started thinking about suicide.

359
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,000
Why are you stabbing yourself?

360
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:05,520
Let go!

361
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,440
What are you doing?

362
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:07,360
Let go!

363
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:08,200
- Let go!
- What are you doing?

364
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:10,080
Let go!

365
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:10,840
Let go!

366
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:13,080
What are you doing?

367
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:14,440
Stop!

368
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,280
Let go!

369
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:17,320
Stop it!

370
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:19,040
Why are you doing this?

371
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:20,280
Why are you doing this?

372
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:20,960
Let go!

373
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:22,440
Let go! Ji, let go!

374
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,720
No, Ji!

375
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:25,240
Stop!

376
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,600
You and I...

377
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:38,280
we're a lot alike.

378
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:45,240
I think so too.

379
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,320
I won't let anything happen to Dr. Ji.

380
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:21,880
And I won't let anything happen
to Chita.

381
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,080
What kind of mirror is this?

382
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:32,240
What a strange lamp.

383
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:47,080
Why is everything in this house so old?

384
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,560
1981?

385
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,280
I wasn't even born then.

386
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:32,240
(Forest near Lom Kao rice mill)

387
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:50,680
A Nour that can kill Nour?

388
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:48,320
Where are you going?

389
00:31:51,480 --> 00:31:52,080
Stay back.

390
00:31:58,720 --> 00:31:59,200
Go!

391
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:04,320
What is this?

392
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:09,360
Explain this to me.

393
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,040
You knew all along

394
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:15,840
that Nour is real.

395
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,680
You also knew

396
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:20,640
which ones are Nour.

397
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:23,960
So why did you hide it from me?

398
00:32:25,560 --> 00:32:26,560
All this time,

399
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:29,960
what was ever real to you?

400
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,520
And my dad's photo.

401
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:35,960
Why was it there?

402
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:40,000
You put it there, didn't you?

403
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:44,160
And the blood in the fridge...

404
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:47,120
Whose blood is it?

405
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:49,280
Where did you get it?

406
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:55,400
All this time,

407
00:32:57,040 --> 00:32:58,240
why have you been lying to me?

408
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,000
I never lied to you.

409
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:18,000
You were behind all this, weren't you?

410
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:20,200
Answer me.

411
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:24,480
You did this, didn't you?

412
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:25,840
Say something!

413
00:33:30,200 --> 00:33:31,680
Why did you do this?

414
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:39,080
Satisfied?

415
00:33:44,120 --> 00:33:45,040
All this time,

416
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:48,720
why did you trick me into loving you?

417
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:02,360
I didn't kill any of those people,

418
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,040
including your father.

419
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:11,000
I took that blood from a corpse.

420
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,480
I'm also hunting the Nour
who killed all those people.

421
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:22,320
Then why did you hide all of this?

422
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,640
Why act like you always
had something to hide?

423
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:29,120
I don't trust anyone.

424
00:34:29,720 --> 00:34:31,600
And I don't need to trust anyone.

425
00:34:35,600 --> 00:34:37,360
But didn't you say
we should trust each other?

426
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:44,440
You just won't admit

427
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:46,480
you've fallen for me.

428
00:34:55,640 --> 00:34:56,240
Right?

429
00:34:58,200 --> 00:34:59,200
You've fallen for me.

430
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:25,600
I'm sorry.

431
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:33,920
It's the only way I can show my love.

432
00:36:46,720 --> 00:36:47,760
I'm sorry.

433
00:37:00,480 --> 00:37:01,960
It's okay, Inspector Ken.

434
00:37:05,560 --> 00:37:06,840
I understand everything now.

435
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:54,800
Are you okay?

436
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:02,440
I'm sorry.

437
00:41:03,560 --> 00:41:05,160
I reported your situation to HQ.

438
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:08,640
I didn't want you to get hurt

439
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:11,920
or get involved with Nour again.

440
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:14,240
Mm.

441
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:15,760
I understand.

442
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,440
Then do you love me?

443
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:20,800
Earlier,

444
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:22,440
you didn't answer me.

445
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:25,760
Of course I do.

446
00:41:26,240 --> 00:41:27,120
If you love me,

447
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:29,640
you can't send me away again.

448
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:32,800
I love you too.

449
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:35,840
I don't want to leave you either.

450
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:38,600
Even if you're Nour

451
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:40,040
and you'll never die,

452
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,440
I still want to stay with you
as long as I can.

453
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:53,760
Then how could you shoot me?

454
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:56,400
How did you know I was Nour?

455
00:42:00,040 --> 00:42:01,600
I can see people's soul colors.

456
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:05,200
Soul colors?

457
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:09,640
They're like an aura around each person.

458
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:11,960
Tee's color,

459
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:15,000
the color of that Nour,

460
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,080
and your color

461
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,560
are all the same.

462
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:20,960
That's how I knew

463
00:42:21,520 --> 00:42:23,040
you weren't an ordinary person.

464
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,440
So you just shot me?

465
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,160
I didn't hit anything vital.

466
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:38,200
I finally get it

467
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:40,640
why you

468
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:42,520
wanted to kill me.

469
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:45,440
Because my color

470
00:42:45,920 --> 00:42:48,000
matches your father's killer's color.

471
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:49,400
Mm.

472
00:42:50,080 --> 00:42:50,760
I'm sorry.

473
00:42:56,720 --> 00:42:58,440
Leaving me in the car yesterday

474
00:43:00,040 --> 00:43:01,120
hurt way more than that bullet.

475
00:43:06,800 --> 00:43:07,720
Inspector.

476
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:11,520
I promise you,

477
00:43:12,440 --> 00:43:13,280
from now on,

478
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:15,680
no matter what happens,

479
00:43:16,960 --> 00:43:18,280
I'll never leave you.

480
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:21,240
Please trust me.

481
00:43:26,040 --> 00:43:27,680
You have to trust me too.

482
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:30,640
Of course.

483
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:38,600
So now,

484
00:43:39,320 --> 00:43:40,480
you think Prae

485
00:43:41,120 --> 00:43:42,600
is the Nour killing
other Nour

486
00:43:43,200 --> 00:43:45,120
and is behind all of this, right?

487
00:43:47,440 --> 00:43:49,400
Now we just need to find her

488
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:51,760
and catch her.

489
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:53,520
(The Nour That Can Kill Nour)

490
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:58,920
Don't worry, Inspector.

491
00:44:01,080 --> 00:44:02,640
I'll help you close this case.

492
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:15,000
(The Nour That Can Kill Nour)

493
00:44:20,840 --> 00:44:22,520
Have you ever dated anyone before?

494
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:25,640
I have.

495
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:27,800
It was a long time ago.

496
00:44:29,280 --> 00:44:29,800
So...

497
00:44:29,960 --> 00:44:31,120
why did you break up?

498
00:44:37,680 --> 00:44:38,280
He lied to me.

499
00:44:43,560 --> 00:44:44,840
Maybe I was just too naive,

500
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:46,240
and that's why he fooled me.

501
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:54,520
It's amazing that we found each other.

502
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:57,160
Then...

503
00:44:58,120 --> 00:44:59,480
let's start fresh from now on.

504
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:05,680
This is my dorm.

505
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:07,560
See you tomorrow.

506
00:45:11,080 --> 00:45:12,760
Want me to stay a little longer?

507
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:17,640
Aren't you in a hurry to get home,
Dr. Ji?

508
00:45:18,680 --> 00:45:20,360
You've been busy all day.

509
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:25,400
I'm not.

510
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:28,960
Just being with you longer

511
00:45:29,360 --> 00:45:30,240
makes me happy.

512
00:45:34,360 --> 00:45:34,680
Okay.

513
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:40,240
See you tomorrow.

514
00:46:04,920 --> 00:46:05,400
Bye.

515
00:46:07,360 --> 00:46:07,840
Okay.

516
00:46:08,960 --> 00:46:09,760
Go ahead.

517
00:46:10,840 --> 00:46:12,000
You go ahead.

518
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:16,880
Okay.

519
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:26,840
I'll get going, then.

520
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:44,560
Bye.

521
00:46:45,080 --> 00:46:45,480
Okay.

522
00:47:15,760 --> 00:47:20,200
♪In a love that can never be real♪

523
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:27,400
♪You gaze in my soul
and share what I feel♪

524
00:47:29,840 --> 00:47:34,680
♪Gray days all fade away, I'm healed♪

525
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:41,600
♪My dull world starts to glow and shine♪

526
00:47:44,080 --> 00:47:50,400
♪Bound by fate we cannot break♪
♪Silent thoughts we both share♪

527
00:47:51,080 --> 00:47:56,840
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

528
00:47:57,640 --> 00:48:02,960
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

529
00:48:05,200 --> 00:48:10,160
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

530
00:48:12,240 --> 00:48:18,480
♪Though this hope can never
reach the ground♪

531
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:23,920
♪You painted hues in my barren land♪

532
00:48:27,880 --> 00:48:34,600
♪In lonely nights I used to fall♪
♪Till your eyes broke through my shell♪

533
00:48:35,240 --> 00:48:41,240
♪Hidden love we dare not tell♪
♪Sweet moments time can't quell♪

534
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:50,360
♪Bound by fate we cannot break♪
♪Silent thoughts we both share♪

535
00:48:51,040 --> 00:48:56,760
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

536
00:48:57,880 --> 00:49:03,480
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

537
00:49:05,480 --> 00:49:10,560
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

538
00:49:12,560 --> 00:49:18,920
♪Though this hope can never
reach the ground♪

539
00:49:19,240 --> 00:49:24,560
♪You painted hues in my barren land♪

540
00:49:54,840 --> 00:49:59,720
♪Wish stays locked inside my heart♪

541
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:08,080
♪Colored memories never depart♪

542
00:50:09,440 --> 00:50:14,800
♪Love that's doomed yet stole my heart♪
